                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers[/h1]\n[i]Please note: I received a free Steam key through the Steam Curator Connect program.[/i]\n\nYou can view my review & gameplay here: https://youtu.be/rJ32s_mm0pg\n\nThis is a good collection of mini-games for VR. This game is perfect for those looking for a party game in VR to play with friends over a few beers. There are 25 mini-games total. The mini-games are quick & zany for the most part. Obviously, some of the mini-games are more fun than others. Most were solid fun. You can play solo (challenges) or local multiplayer (tournament).\n\nI liked the visual presentation. The game ran smoothly and the art style is good for this type of game genre. However, this game lacks an announcer or VOs of any kind. The mini-games start suddenly and end quickly, some a little too quick. I would have liked to seen an improved pacing overall. Some of the mini-games would have been better if they had just lasted like 15-20 seconds longer. I think that adding an announcer VO to this game would have greatly improved the experience.\n\nI didn't experience any issues. I think the shooting mechanic in the gun mini-games could be improved. Some of the throwing physics could be a bit better as well. Still, this is one of the better VR party mini-game collections out there. \n\n[b]Rate 7/10.[/b]",
